  "latestMilestone": "Canonical SWIR_OS main now includes the verified native GTK4 SWIR Backup & Restore foundation for signed-in-user SWIR state. It backs up only the allowlisted SWIR config and app-data roots into bounded owner-only archives with a manifest and per-file SHA-256 integrity checks; symlinks, special files, traversal, duplicate or unmanifested members, encrypted members, oversize payloads and digest mismatches fail closed. Restore performs full verification and disposable staging before live-root replacement, requires separate explicit confirmation in the UI, preserves the previous roots as recovery directories and exercises rollback on an injected partial-commit failure. Dedicated hostile-input/rollback tests, a real Wayland GTK4 create-mutate-restore E2E cycle and the exact Debian 13 target runtime all passed on the PR head, together with the System Edition, Live USB, graphical-session and full-installer gates. The authoritative roadmap intentionally remains 55/65 (84.6%) because the broader essential native daily-use application suite is still incomplete. Physical Live USB qualification remains pending; Secure Boot and legacy BIOS are not claimed.",
